<!-- Earnings Statement, banded-panel layout: grey full-bleed section bands separating
     a boxed company block, a two-column employee detail grid, side-by-side payment and
     deduction panels, and a right-aligned pair of total boxes.

     Two structural devices carry this design:
       - a panel box is a COLUMN with a border, so the tables stacked inside it compose
         into one outlined card and flex stretch keeps both panels the same height;
       - optional rows (overtime, bonus, state paid leave) are their own tables with
         renderIf, since renderIf drops a table but cannot drop a single row. Every one
         of those tables repeats the same fixed column widths so the stack stays aligned.

     Figures use format="currency" — this form prints a dollar sign. -->
